        "original_id": "98220feb-b5a6-529d-becc-e6246b342b7b",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Brent Hodge, Harley Knoles, Thomas Buchan, Jon Siddall, Sheila Peacock, Clara Beranger, David Graham Phillips\n- Roles: documentary filmmaker, entrepreneur, film director, producer, writer\n- Films: The Beetle Roadtrip Sessions, A Brony Tale, Winning America, The Cost\n- Awards: Shorty Awards\n\nFacts:\n- Harley Knoles, also known as Harry Knoles, was a British film director of the silent era who lived from 1880 to 1936.\n- The Cost is a 1920 American silent drama film directed by Harley Knoles and written by Clara Beranger and David Graham Phillips.\n- Brent Hodge was born on July 9, 1985 and is a Canadian-New Zealander documentary filmmaker and entrepreneur.\n- Brent Hodge was nominated for Shorty Awards in the director category in 2014 for The Beetle Roadtrip Sessions and in 2015 for A Brony Tale.\n- Winning America was directed by Brent Hodge and Thomas Buchan and produced by Brent Hodge, Jon Siddall, and Sheila Peacock.",
